{"tool_name":"makehub","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"makehub","identifiers":["doi:10.1101/550145"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"MakeHub is a command line tool for the fully automatic generation of of track data hubs for visualizing genomes with the UCSC genome browser.","home_url":"https://github.com/Gaius-Augustus/MakeHub","keywords":["Genomics","RNA-Seq","Functional genomics","Sequence Alignment"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"makehub","home":"https://github.com/Gaius-Augustus/MakeHub","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Fully Automated Generation of UCSC Genome Browser Assembly Hubs.\nMakeHub is a command line tool for the fully automatic generation of of track data hubs1 for visualizing genomes with the UCSC genome browser2. Track data hubs are data structures that contain all required information about a genome for visualizing with the UCSC genome browser.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T07:29:12Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-19T09:15:43Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:makehub","edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genome annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0362"},{"term":"Genome visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3208"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"MakeHub","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/J.GPB.2019.05.003","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 The AuthorNovel genomes are today often annotated by small consortia or individuals whose background is not from bioinformatics. This audience requires tools that are easy to use. Such need has been addressed by several genome annotation tools and pipelines. Visualizing resulting annotation is a crucial step of quality control. The UCSC Genome Browser is a powerful and popular genome visualization tool. Assembly Hubs, which can be hosted on any publicly available web server, allow browsing genomes via UCSC Genome Browser servers. The steps for creating custom Assembly Hubs are well documented and the required tools are publicly available. However, the number of steps for creating a novel Assembly Hub is large. In some cases, the format of input files needs to be adapted, which is a difficult task for scientists without programming background. Here, we describe MakeHub, a novel command line tool that generates Assembly Hubs for the UCSC Genome Browser in a fully automated fashion. The pipeline also allows extending previously created Hubs by additional tracks. MakeHub is freely available for downloading at https://github.com/Gaius-Augustus/MakeHub.","authors":[{"name":"Hoff K.J."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2019-10-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genomics, Proteomics and Bioinformatics","title":"MakeHub: Fully Automated Generation of UCSC Genome Browser Assembly Hubs"},"pmcid":"PMC7056914","pmid":"32001327"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene transcripts","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3512"},{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"MakeHub","home":"https://bio.tools/makehub","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Fully Automated Generation of UCSC Genome Browser Assembly Hubs.\nMakeHub is a command line tool for the fully automatic generation of of track data hubs1 for visualizing genomes with the UCSC genome browser2. Track data hubs are data structures that contain all required information about a genome for visualizing with the UCSC genome browser.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:makehub/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated"